  "details": "adding a OnParticleCollision to the vrc trigger component could be used to detect particle collision events. \"OnParticleCollision is called when a particle hits a Collider.\"  \"This message is sent to all scripts attached to the WorldParticleCollider and to the Collider that was hit.\" this could be used to make a very simple efficient gun or trigger sound vfx when hitting something. it should be easy to implement since its using the manobehaviour.onpariclecollision class ( https://docs.unity3d.com/560/Documentation/ScriptReference/MonoBehaviour.OnParticleCollision.html ).",
